# flash of the arduino-mega-2560 fixture board: connect-mega2560, then write-mega2560
# Arduino Mega 2560 (ATmega16U2, the wiring bootloader at 115200): DTR pulse, CMD_SIGN_ON, then
# CMD_READ_SIGNATURE_ISP for each signature byte
! identity 2341:0042
! baud 115200
! signals dtr=0 rts=0
! sleep 250
! signals dtr=1 rts=1
! sleep 50
> 1b 01 00 01 0e 01 14
< 1b 01 00 0b 0e 01 00 08 "AVRISP_2" 74
> 1b 02 00 06 0e 1b 04 30 00 00 00 3e
< 1b 02 00 04 0e 1b 00 1e 00 16
> 1b 03 00 06 0e 1b 04 30 00 01 00 3e
< 1b 03 00 04 0e 1b 00 98 00 91
> 1b 04 00 06 0e 1b 04 30 00 02 00 3a
< 1b 04 00 04 0e 1b 00 01 00 0f
# After connect-mega2560 (messages 1 to 4): avr-application.hex (300 bytes at 0) written in two
# 256-byte pages (CMD_LOAD_ADDRESS with bit 31 set, CMD_PROGRAM_FLASH_ISP, the last page padded
# with ff), read back page by page (CMD_READ_FLASH_ISP), then CMD_LEAVE_PROGMODE_ISP. Written by
# session() of tests/avr.rs.
